IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ja-juror`
IMPORT `ja-qa`

-- Juries Act 1957 (WA) -- cases for the Q&A layer (ja-qa.l4): every exported question, for every role and every
-- situation.
--
-- Each question is asked for the role it is not about, with every other input an ASSUMEd value that has none: the
-- answer must be `does not arise for you`, and reading any of those inputs would stop the evaluation with an error ("it
-- is an assumed term"). Each question that takes a situation input is asked, for its own role, with FALSE and every
-- later input ASSUMEd: again `does not arise for you`. For the person summonsed (the baseline's seat) each answer is
-- also asserted equal to the baseline export's own answer on the same facts. Expected values are worked by hand from
-- the deposited text, never copied from the output.
--
-- Facts: Chloe (c025, c077) and her employer Jarrah Legal Technologies Pty Ltd, as in the baseline's cases
-- (ja-cases-juror.l4), whose fixtures are restated here. Figures marked HYPOTHETICAL are the baseline's.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases -- the Q&A layer`

ASSUME `an unasked fact` IS A BOOLEAN
ASSUME `an unasked number` IS A NUMBER
ASSUME `an unasked person` IS A Person
ASSUME `an unasked trial` IS A TrialKind
ASSUME `unasked circumstances` IS A Circumstances
ASSUME `an unasked cause` IS A GoodReasonCause
ASSUME `an unasked decider` IS A Decider
ASSUME `an unasked summons` IS A SummonsKind
ASSUME `an unasked act` IS AN EmployerAction
ASSUME `an unasked recipient` IS A FeeRecipient
ASSUME `an unasked telling` IS A WhatITell
ASSUME `an unasked listener` IS A WhoITell
ASSUME `an unasked act of mine` IS A `What I did to my employee`

`as the juror` MEANS `I am liable for jury service, or have been summonsed for it`
`as the employer` MEANS `I employ someone who has been summonsed for jury service`

`a 3-year prison term in 2010` MEANS Conviction WITH
    `the sentence` IS `imprisonment for a term`
    `months of imprisonment` IS 36
    `it was quashed or set aside` IS FALSE
    `I was pardoned for it` IS FALSE
    `it is spent` IS FALSE
    `it was in Western Australia` IS TRUE
    `it was within the relevant period` IS FALSE
    `its statutory penalty includes imprisonment` IS TRUE
    `it was against a road law` IS FALSE

`an 18-month prison term in 2010` MEANS Conviction WITH
    `the sentence` IS `imprisonment for a term`
    `months of imprisonment` IS 18
    `it was quashed or set aside` IS FALSE
    `I was pardoned for it` IS FALSE
    `it is spent` IS FALSE
    `it was in Western Australia` IS TRUE
    `it was within the relevant period` IS FALSE
    `its statutory penalty includes imprisonment` IS TRUE
    `it was against a road law` IS FALSE

GIVEN `age` IS A NUMBER
      `enrolled` IS A BOOLEAN
      `provisional` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the class` IS A Schedule1Class
      `convictions` IS A LIST OF Conviction
      `on bail` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Person
`a person aged` MEANS
    Person WITH
        `I am enrolled to vote at Legislative Assembly elections` IS `enrolled`
        `I am enrolled only provisionally because I am under 18` IS `provisional`
        `I am kept on the roll as an eligible overseas elector` IS FALSE
        `I am enrolled as an itinerant elector` IS FALSE
        `my age` IS `age`
        `my Schedule 1 class` IS `the class`
        `my convictions` IS `convictions`
        `in the relevant period I was serving a prison sentence or on parole` IS FALSE
        `in the relevant period I was found guilty and detained as a juvenile offender` IS FALSE
        `in the relevant period I was on a probation order or community order` IS FALSE
        `I am on bail or in custody awaiting trial or sentence` IS `on bail`
        `I am an involuntary patient under the Mental Health Act 2014` IS FALSE
        `I am a represented person under the Guardianship and Administration Act 1990` IS FALSE
        `I am a person covered by the Criminal Law (Mental Impairment) Act 2023` IS FALSE

`Chloe summonsed at 33 (c077)` MEANS `a person aged` 33 TRUE FALSE `none of the Schedule 1 classes` EMPTY FALSE
`a 16-year-old enrolled provisionally` MEANS `a person aged` 16 TRUE TRUE `none of the Schedule 1 classes` EMPTY FALSE
`a retiree aged 75` MEANS `a person aged` 75 TRUE FALSE `none of the Schedule 1 classes` EMPTY FALSE
`a police officer` MEANS `a person aged` 40 TRUE FALSE `a member of the WA Police or a police cadet` EMPTY FALSE
`someone given 3 years in 2010` MEANS `a person aged` 40 TRUE FALSE `none of the Schedule 1 classes` (LIST `a 3-year prison term in 2010`) FALSE
`someone given 18 months in 2010` MEANS `a person aged` 40 TRUE FALSE `none of the Schedule 1 classes` (LIST `an 18-month prison term in 2010`) FALSE
`someone on bail awaiting trial` MEANS `a person aged` 40 TRUE FALSE `none of the Schedule 1 classes` EMPTY TRUE

`nothing else` MEANS Circumstances WITH
    `I hold a certificate permanently excusing me` IS FALSE
    `the Jury Exemption Act 1965 says I shall not be summoned` IS FALSE
    `I do not live in the jury district` IS FALSE
    `my English may not be good enough to serve effectively` IS FALSE
    `a physical disability or mental impairment may stop me serving effectively` IS FALSE
    `there is a reason I may not be indifferent between the parties` IS FALSE

-- Mirror cases (c077): Jarrah threatens Chloe's job over her summons, asked from her seat and from Jarrah's.
#ASSERT `Does my employer commit an offence by what it did to me` `as the juror` TRUE `threatens to end my employment or cut or stop my pay or otherwise prejudice me` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence by what I did to my employee` `as the employer` `I threaten to end their employment, cut or stop their pay or otherwise prejudice them` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS yes
-- ... Jarrah keeps paying her: the fees go to Jarrah, from both seats.
#ASSERT `Who does the State pay my jury service fees to` `as the juror` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the answer is` `my employer`
#ASSERT `Do I get the State's jury service fees for my employee` `as the employer` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS yes
-- ... and neither can excuse her.
#ASSERT `Can my employer excuse me from my summons` `as the juror` TRUE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `May I excuse my employee from jury service` `as the employer` EQUALS no
-- The employer's words map to the baseline's, value for value (the helper lists every value).
#ASSERT `in the employee's words` `I stop paying them` EQUALS `stops paying me`
#ASSERT `in the employee's words` `I otherwise prejudice them in their employment` EQUALS `otherwise prejudices me in my employment`
#ASSERT `in the employee's words` `I threaten not to pay them those earnings` EQUALS `threatens not to pay me those earnings`
#ASSERT `in the employee's words` `I do nothing adverse` EQUALS `nothing adverse`

